      "rule": "R19",
      "severity": "must",
      "text": "The specification says indexes are checked in creation order, but SQLite checks ordinary unique indexes in reverse creation order: on pinned SQLite 3.51.0, inserting duplicate `(1,1)` into `t(a UNIQUE,b UNIQUE)` reports `t.b`, consistent with [SQLite’s source](https://www3.sqlite.org/matrix/ev/src/build.html). Fix: change “the order of creation” to “reverse creation order” while retaining the REPLACE and UPSERT qualifications."
    }
